s.00124.2005</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Leung</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Sharp</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Function and localization of microRNAs in mammalian cells.</article-title><source>Cold Spring Harb Symp Quant Biol</source><year>2006</year><volume>71</volume><fpage>29</fpage><lpage>38</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17381277</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1101/sqb.2006.71.049</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Selvaraj</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Prywes</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Expression profiling of serum inducible genes identifies a subset of SRF target genes that are MKL dependent.</article-title><source>BMC Mol Biol</source><year>2004</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>13</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15329155</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1471-2199-5-13</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Glauser</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Brun</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Gauthier</surname><given-names>BR</given-names></name><name><surname>Schlegel</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transcriptional response of pancreatic &#x003b2; cells to metabolic stimulation: large scale identification of immediate-early and secondary response genes.</article-title><source>BMC Mol Biol</source><year>2007</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>54</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17587450</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1471-2199-8-54</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Amit</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Citri</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Shay</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Lu</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Katz</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Tarcic</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>siwak</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Lahad</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacob-Birsch</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Amariglio</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Vaisman</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Segal</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Rechavi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Alon</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Mills</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name><name><surname>Domany</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Yarden</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A module of negative feedback regulators defines growth factor signaling.</article-title><source>Nat Genet</source><year>2007</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>503</fpage><lpage>512</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17322878</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/ng1987</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sugden</surname><given-names>PH</given-names></name><name><surname>Clerk</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cellular mechanisms of cardiac hypertrophy.</article-title><source>J Mol Med</source><year>1998</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>725</fpage><lpage>746</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9826118</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s001090050275</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sugden</surname><given-names>PH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An overview of endothelin signaling in the cardiac myocyte.</article-title><source>J Mol Cell Cardiol</source><year>2003</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>871</fpage><lpage>886</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12878473</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0022-2828(03)00153-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bueno</surname><given-names>OF</given-names></name><name><surname>De Windt</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Tymitz</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Witt</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kimball</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>Klevitsky</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Hewett</surname><given-names>TE</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Lefer</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Peng</surname><given-names>C-F</given-names></name><name><surname>Kitsis</surname><given-names>RN</given-names></name><name><surname>Molkentin</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The MEK1-ERK1/2 signaling pathway promotes compensated cardiac hypertrophy in transgenic mice.</article-title><source>EMBO J</source><year>2000</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>6341</fpage><lpage>6350</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11101507</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/emboj/19.23.6341</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heineke</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Molkentin</surname><given-name